        // The C contract's onlyPool modifier checks iPOOLFACTORY(_DAO().POOLFACTORY()).isCuratedPool(msg.sender) == true
        // but in our test harness the easiest route is to bypass that restriction by impersonating DEPLOYER when deploying C.
        // However, per instructions, c is already deployed in setUp as new C(address(this), address(this)).
        // We will simulate the allowed pool behavior by directly calling c.mintSynth via vm.prank from the pool address.
        // The test focuses on ensuring that a read-only call to allowance(...) does not change mapSynth_LPBalance[pool].

        // Record pre-call value of mapSynth_LPBalance for pool
        uint256 before = c.getmapAddress_LPBalance(pool);

        // Now perform an external sequence that may affect state in correct contract: call mintSynth as if from pool
        // to create a situation where the mutant (which fails to credit LP balance) would diverge.
        // We need pool to be able to call mintSynth; the contract's onlyPool modifier in C checks an external factory,
        // which in our test environment will NOT recognize arbitrary 'pool' as curated, so mintSynth would revert.
